message: "If you use this formalisation in your research, please cite it as follows."
title: "M4TH: Formalised PDE and Analytic Number Theory in Lean 4"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21635317
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-28
authors:
  - family-names: Izquierdo Perez
    given-names: Bezalel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5993-4057"
    alias: Alektronnik
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alektronnik/M4TH"
url: "https://github.com/Alektronnik/M4TH"
abstract: >
  Self-contained formalisation in Lean 4 over Mathlib of elementary PDE theory
  and analytic number theory. Seven independent packages across two releases:
  v1.0.0 -- ConservationLaws (weak solutions, travelling shocks, Rankine-Hugoniot,
  Lax entropy condition for arbitrary flux), BurgersBlowUp (finite-time gradient
  blow-up via exact Riccati solution), KdV (exact one-soliton profile and
  conservation laws). v2.0.0 -- DirichletEta (Dirichlet eta function and
  non-vanishing of zeta on (0,1)), ZetaZeroCounting (Riemann-von Mangoldt N(T)
  with safe height enclosures), XiLogResidue (logarithmic residue = multiplicity,
  dictionary with MeromorphicOn.divisor), XiLogDeriv (expansion of the xi
  log-derivative and digamma identity for GammaR). Zero axioms, zero sorry.
  Every headline theorem carries the clean axiom certificate [propext,
  Classical.choice, Quot.sound].
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - partial differential equations
  - conservation laws
  - Rankine-Hugoniot
  - Burgers equation
  - gradient blow-up
  - KdV equation
  - solitons
  - Riemann zeta function
  - zero counting
  - von Mangoldt
  - Dirichlet eta
  - logarithmic residue
  - digamma
  - analytic number theory
